From: TechNet <local>
Subject: [PATCH] manager: Leave WoWLAN Wi-Fi connected on wake

A Wi-Fi device kept associated through suspend by WoWLAN was still taken down
and re-activated on every resume, dropping the link for about 13s on Thor.
Wi-Fi already notices a lost association through the supplicant, so skip the
takedown for it and keep it for wired Wake-on-LAN devices.
---
--- a/src/core/nm-manager.c
+++ b/src/core/nm-manager.c
@@ -7373,7 +7373,8 @@
                 /* Belatedly take down Wake-on-LAN devices; ideally we wouldn't have to do this
                  * but for now it's the only way to make sure we re-check their connectivity.
                  */
-                if (device_is_wake_on_lan(priv->platform, device))
+                if (device_is_wake_on_lan(priv->platform, device)
+                    && nm_device_get_device_type(device) != NM_DEVICE_TYPE_WIFI)
                     nm_device_set_unmanaged_by_flags(device,
                                                      NM_UNMANAGED_MANAGER_DISABLED,
                                                      NM_UNMAN_FLAG_OP_SET_UNMANAGED,
